<h2>The Basics of Vim</h2>
<p>On this webpage I will go over the basics on how to use vim.<br>Here I will talk about how to open and close vim and how to save files. I will also create a list of useful commands that you can use in vim:</p>
<h4>Opening/Closing vim</h4>
<p>To open and close vim you will need to:</p>
<ol>
<li>Get to your desktop.
 <ul>You can navigate your computer by using the "cd" command, so to get to your desktop just type in "cd Desktop" in your terminal.
</ul>
</li>
<li>Next Get to your website
<ul>Doing this is the same as getting to the desktop, just use "cd website".
</ul>
</li>
<li>Now that you are in your website you can open vim.<br>To do this type vim and then your folders name.
</ol>
<p>Amazing! Now we are in vim.</p>
<h4>Saving Files in vim</h4>
<p>Saving files in vim is quick and easy.<br>To do it all you have to do is
<ol>
<li>Press the escape key on your computer</li>
<li>Type :wq and press enter
</ol>
<p>Great! We are done here</p>
